Contour: edge light and fillets (edge_light, mask_fillet), a sheet that wells
out of the layer it hangs from.

- hg.layer(..., { edge_light = 0.55 }): the pane's edge drawn as light. A
  crisp line on the traced outline with a short tail and a slightly darker
  band just inside it, lit from the upper left: brightest on edges facing up,
  towards the left, less on those facing down, towards the right, a fifth on
  the sides. Clear glass over dark ground has nothing to bend and shows by
  this line alone. It reads the distance field, so it follows the outline
  frame by frame as the app animates it and leaves open and joined edges
  out. A nested shape keeps its own rim line. On a mask_open layer the light
  is placed across the layer it continues, so both carry it as one pane and
  the line of one runs into the line of the other.
- The outline is traced round every texel the app covers at all, a good
  pixel outside the edge that shows: the line starts that far in
  (OUTLINE_INSET_PX).
- hg.layer(..., { mask_open = "top", mask_fillet = 22 }): where the shape's
  side meets its open edge the seed pass adds a fillet of that radius (logical
  px) to the shape, and within those rows the glass is cut by the outline
  instead of by the app's alpha. The side is read one radius in from the
  edge, so the fillet does not depend on what the app draws there: Noctalia
  slides a panel out from under the bar and shows its own fillets only once
  it has arrived, which left square inner corners all the way down and a pop
  at the end.
- The fillet starts on the edge of the layer the shape hangs from, not on
  the box's (the boxes overlap by a row), so the outline leaves that edge at
  a tangent.
- mask_join now reads the other layer's distance between its texels and at
  the row the two boxes really meet on (it assumed they abut, and stepped by
  that field's whole texels, which put a jog into the edge where it turns
  into a fillet), and counts that shape only where it is at least 1.75 px deep:
  a fillet's tip is a sliver too thin to show an edge of its own, and this
  layer's edge runs on beside it until it does. With edge_light on both
  layers one line then bends from the bar's edge into the fillet.
- The light's numbers are those of the ACID//HUD pane light (quickshell hud,
  shaders/pane.frag), which draws it for layers the HUD owns.

