 `open_frost` lets the glass thicken as it runs on: at the open edge it is the layer's own glass, the same as the one it continues, and over `open_feather` logical px it turns into frosted glass, blurred by that much more (in `blur_strength` units). The seam stays invisible, and a window edge right behind it dissolves instead of reading as a line. Top and bottom open edges only.
 
+`mask_fillet` rounds the inner corners a `mask_open` shape makes with the layer it hangs from: where its side meets the open edge, the outline sweeps out in a quarter circle of that radius, and the glass fills it. It starts on the edge of the layer the shape hangs from (the boxes may overlap by a row), so the outline leaves that edge at a tangent, and that layer's `mask_join` follows it between texels: with `edge_light` on both, one line bends from the edge into the fillet. The side is read one radius in from the edge, so the fillet is the same whether or not the app draws one itself. A panel that slides out from under a bar and shows its own fillets only when it has arrived then has them from the first frame; set the radius the app uses and nothing moves when its own appear.
+
+`edge_light` draws the pane's edge as light: a crisp line on the traced outline with a short tail and a slightly darker band just inside it, lit from the upper left (brightest on edges facing up, less on those facing down, a fifth on the sides). Clear glass over a dark backdrop has nothing to bend and shows by this line alone. It follows the outline as the app animates it and leaves open and joined edges out, so a `mask_open` panel carries the line down its sides and round its corners from the layer it hangs from. Give both layers the same `edge_light`: the light then falls on the two as one pane, and the line of the one runs into the line of the other where their outlines meet.
+
 **Cost:** none for layers that do not use it. For a layer that does, one extra texture read per glass pixel, and a few short GPU passes and a few MB of memory while a contour layer exists (shared work buffers included), freed when the last one closes or stops using `contour`. `hyprctl hyprglass stats` counts the rebuilds (`contour_build`).
 
 **Fixed shape:** `shape` gives a layer's glass its own rounded box, so a floating bar or a card inside a larger layer gets its own edge, bend and highlights instead of those of the whole layer. `inset` trims the layer's edges (one value, or top, right, bottom, left) and `radius` rounds the corners, `-1` for a pill; both in logical px (up to 16384), and a negative inset reaches past that edge. Content outside the shape is still drawn, without glass. Inside it, `mask_mode` still decides where the glass goes: set the layer's `mask_threshold` to `0` to fill the whole shape.
